					"item": {
						"id": "minecraft:written_book"
						"Count": 1b
						"tag": {
							"title": "红木事件"
							"author": "The National Gazette"
							"pages": [
								"{\"text\": \"THE NATIONAL GAZETTE\\nThe Redwood Incident\\n\\nOfficials have\\nconfirmed the total\\nfailure of the\\nRedwood Containment\\nZone. Cities now stand\\nabandoned and silent.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"The Redwood Program\\nwas established to\\nisolate hostile entities\\ndiscovered in the\\nforest. For seventy\\nyears, fences,\\nsensors and armed\\npatrols held the\\nperimeter.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"That changed when an\\nunauthorized person\\ncrossed the perimeter\\nand disappeared into\\nthe forest. The\\nintruder was later\\nidentified as an\\nescapee from\\nAshgrove Psychiatric\\nHospital.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"Military sources say\\nthe person carried no\\nequipment and wore no\\nuniform. Yet they\\nbegan broadcasting\\nmessages claiming to\\nbe a ranger\\ninvestigating strange\\nsightings. The\\ntransmissions\\ncontinued for weeks.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"Within hours of the\\ncrossing, containment\\nsystems began to fail.\\nDays later, figures\\nappeared in nearby\\ntowns: human-shaped,\\nbut wrong. Farms\\nemptied overnight.\\nStreets fell silent\\nexcept for whispers.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"The military\\nresponded with air\\nstrikes, firebombing\\nand sealed quarantine\\nzones. Nothing held.\\nCheckpoints fell.\\nEntire units\\ndisappeared without a\\nshot being fired.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"Within two weeks,\\nmajor cities reported\\nblackouts, panic and\\nmass casualties.\\nEmergency\\nbroadcasts dissolved\\ninto overlapping\\nvoices and static\\nbefore falling silent.\"}"
								"{\"text\": \"This edition was\\nprinted before our\\nnewsroom was\\nevacuated. The Office\\nof Civil Defence has\\nissued no further\\nupdates.\"}"
							]
							"redwood_revision": 6
						}
					}
					"title": "红木事件"
				}
			]
